From: AdrielOrihuela <adriel.orihuela.m@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:10:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Build Bukkit's, Spigot's and Paper's files in memory from the
 TOML files

bukkit.yml, commands.yml, spigot.yml, paper-global.yml,
paper-world-defaults.yml and each world's paper-world.yml stop existing
on disk. Their content comes from the TOML files in config/, through the
objects LegacyFolia's bridge builds, and nothing here loads or saves any
of them any more:

- CraftServer takes configuration and commandsConfiguration from the
  bridge, in its constructor, in reload() and in reloadCommandAliases(),
  and no longer has saveConfig or saveCommandsConfig.
- SpigotConfig is initialised with the built configuration on reload and
  by /spigot reload, with a section for every loaded world.
- Paper's global node, its world-defaults node and each world's node are
  the bridge's nodes copied into a node of Paper's own loader, so they
  carry Paper's serializers; the version check and the transformations
  run as before, and the save, the template file Paper created for each
  world and the read-back of the defaults from disk are gone. The world
  defaults stay in memory where Paper used to save them for each world
  to read back. A world's section in worlds.toml is found by its folder
  name, which a new context key carries.
- Bukkit.spigot().getPaperConfig() is assembled from the same nodes.
- /reload, /spigot reload and /paper reload read the TOML files and
  server.properties again first, so an edit is what they pick up.
- The plugin loader, which reads the update folder before the TOML files
  are loaded, reads it in the order the server will settle it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

